# hc-grow: the victim HARVESTS cores from the Secondary (motivation pass 3 add-on, user
# 2026-11-09). Victim on 4 threads 18-21 (configs/motiv3-sm110p-int4.yaml, GOMAXPROCS 4,
# limit 4), HC Primary pool = those 4 threads; the hc-secondary-burner lives on the shared
# threads 20,21 plus its own thread 11 (motiv2/burner-node4-shared.yaml). While the victim is
# quiet HC lends the idle Primary threads to the burner; under overload the victim spreads
# to 20,21, the Monitor sees them busy and the Balancer pulls the burner back to 11.
# hc-hold semantics (applied once at the enable, never released). Compare with none (2-P),
# rep1 (2-P + one 2-P replica) and none on the 4-P victim (4 exclusive cores).
ISO_ACTUATOR=hc
N_MAX=0
HC_VICTIM_CPULIST=18,19,20,21
HC_SECONDARY_CPULIST=11
HC_TARGET_IDLE_CORES=1
HC_LOW_TIC=1
HC_ACBF=0.33
HC_MIN_SECONDARY_CORES=0
HC_BALANCER_CPU=14
HC_THETA_ON=-1
HC_THETA_OFF=-2
HC_UP_WINDOWS=1
HC_DOWN_WINDOWS=1000000
